### BarOps POS - API Test Collection
### Sprint 1: Catalog CRUD & Branch-Level Menu/Stock Management
### This file documents the 5 new endpoint groups for manual testing

### ============================================================================
### SETUP: Authentication (prerequisite for all tests)
### ============================================================================

### 1. Register Owner
POST http://localhost:8080/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "owner@barops.com",
  "password": "Owner123!",
  "fullName": "Owner User",
  "role": "OWNER"
}

### 2. Login Owner (get JWT token)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "owner@barops.com",
  "password": "Owner123!"
}

### Store the token from response and use as: Authorization: Bearer {token}

---

### ============================================================================
### ENDPOINT GROUP 1: CATALOG PRODUCTS (Business-wide)
### ============================================================================
### API Route: /api/products
### Entity: Product (business_id auto-assigned, tenant-scoped)
### No price at catalog level (price is set per-branch in menu items)

### 1.1 Create Product
POST http://localhost:8080/api/products
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer YOUR_OWNER_TOKEN

{
  "name": "Vodka",
  "displayNameEn": "Premium Vodka",
  "isActive": true
}

### Expected: 201 Created, returns ProductResponse with id, name, displayNameEn, isActive, businessId

### 1.2 Create another product (for recipe testing)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/products
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer YOUR_OWNER_TOKEN

{
  "name": "Cranberry Juice",
  "displayNameEn": "Cranberry Juice",
  "isActive": true
}

### 1.3 List Products (with pagination)
GET http://localhost:8080/api/products?page=0&size=20&sort=name,asc
Authorization: Bearer YOUR_OWNER_TOKEN

### Expected: 200 OK, returns Page<ProductResponse> with products from current business only

### 1.4 Get Single Product
GET http://localhost:8080/api/products/1
Authorization: Bearer YOUR_OWNER_TOKEN

### Expected: 200 OK or 404 Not Found if product doesn't exist

### 1.5 Update Product
PUT http://localhost:8080/api/products/1
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer YOUR_OWNER_TOKEN

{
  "name": "Premium Vodka",
  "displayNameEn": "Premium Russian Vodka",
  "isActive": true
}

### Expected: 200 OK, returns updated ProductResponse

### 1.6 Deactivate Product (soft delete)
DELETE http://localhost:8080/api/products/1
Authorization: Bearer YOUR_OWNER_TOKEN

### Expected: 204 No Content
### Note: This also deactivates all menu items for this product across all branches

---

### ============================================================================
### ENDPOINT GROUP 2: CATALOG INGREDIENTS (Business-wide)
### ============================================================================
### API Route: /api/ingredients
### Entity: Ingredient (business_id auto-assigned, tenant-scoped)
### No stock quantity at catalog level (stock is per-branch in BranchIngredientStock)

### 2.1 Create Ingredient
POST http://localhost:8080/api/ingredients
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer YOUR_OWNER_TOKEN

{
  "name": "Vodka",
  "unit": "ML"
}

### Expected: 201 Created, returns IngredientResponse with id, name, unit, businessId

### 2.2 Create more ingredients
POST http://localhost:8080/api/ingredients
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer YOUR_OWNER_TOKEN

{
  "name": "Cranberry Juice",
  "unit": "ML"
}

---

POST http://localhost:8080/api/ingredients
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer YOUR_OWNER_TOKEN

{
  "name": "Lime",
  "unit": "PIECE"
}

### 2.3 List Ingredients (with pagination)
GET http://localhost:8080/api/ingredients?page=0&size=20&sort=name,asc
Authorization: Bearer YOUR_OWNER_TOKEN

### Expected: 200 OK, returns Page<IngredientResponse> with ingredients from current business only

### 2.4 Get Single Ingredient
GET http://localhost:8080/api/ingredients/1
Authorization: Bearer YOUR_OWNER_TOKEN

### Expected: 200 OK or 404 Not Found

### 2.5 Update Ingredient
PUT http://localhost:8080/api/ingredients/1
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer YOUR_OWNER_TOKEN

{
  "name": "Premium Vodka",
  "unit": "ML"
}

### Expected: 200 OK, returns updated IngredientResponse

### 2.6 Delete Ingredient
DELETE http://localhost:8080/api/ingredients/1
Authorization: Bearer YOUR_OWNER_TOKEN

### Expected: 204 No Content
### Note: Will fail (409 Conflict) if ingredient has active recipes or stock records

---

### ============================================================================
### ENDPOINT GROUP 3: RECIPES (Bills of Materials)
### ============================================================================
### API Route: /api/products/{productId}/recipe
### Entity: Recipe (business_id auto-assigned, product_id PK, ingredient_id PK, unique per product)
### Recipe is a join table: Product → Recipe ← Ingredient (with quantity)

### 3.1 Create Recipe (add ingredient to product)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/products/1/recipe
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer YOUR_OWNER_TOKEN

{
  "ingredientId": 1,
  "quantity": 50.0
}

### Expected: 201 Created, returns RecipeResponse with productId, ingredientId, quantity

### 3.2 Add another ingredient to same product
POST http://localhost:8080/api/products/1/recipe
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer YOUR_OWNER_TOKEN

{
  "ingredientId": 2,
  "quantity": 30.0
}

### Expected: 201 Created
### Note: Duplicate ingredientId for same product will fail (409 Conflict)

### 3.3 List Recipe (all ingredients for a product)
GET http://localhost:8080/api/products/1/recipe
Authorization: Bearer YOUR_OWNER_TOKEN

### Expected: 200 OK, returns List<RecipeResponse> with all ingredients for productId=1

### 3.4 Get Single Recipe Entry
GET http://localhost:8080/api/products/1/recipe/1
Authorization: Bearer YOUR_OWNER_TOKEN

### Expected: 200 OK or 404 Not Found (if ingredient not in recipe)

### 3.5 Update Recipe Entry (change ingredient quantity)
PUT http://localhost:8080/api/products/1/recipe/1
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer YOUR_OWNER_TOKEN

{
  "quantity": 60.0
}

### Expected: 200 OK, returns updated RecipeResponse

### 3.6 Delete Recipe Entry (remove ingredient from product)
DELETE http://localhost:8080/api/products/1/recipe/1
Authorization: Bearer YOUR_OWNER_TOKEN

### Expected: 204 No Content
### Note: Soft deletes the recipe entry (sets is_deleted=true or removes record)

---

### ============================================================================
### ENDPOINT GROUP 4: BRANCH MENU ITEMS (Per-Branch Pricing & Availability)
### ============================================================================
### API Route: /api/branches/{branchId}/menu-items
### Entity: BranchMenuItem (branch_id + product_id, branch-scoped)
### This is where pricing and availability are managed

### Prerequisites:
### - Product must exist in catalog (from endpoint group 1)
### - Branch must exist in system (managed by Branch management endpoints)
### - Current user's branchId must match or user is OWNER (branchId = null)

### 4.1 Add Product to Branch Menu (set price and availability)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/branches/1/menu-items
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer YOUR_OWNER_TOKEN

{
  "productId": 1,
  "price": 15.50,
  "available": true
}

### Expected: 201 Created, returns BranchMenuItemResponse with branchId, productId, price, available

### 4.2 Add another product to menu
POST http://localhost:8080/api/branches/1/menu-items
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer YOUR_OWNER_TOKEN

{
  "productId": 2,
  "price": 8.00,
  "available": true
}

### 4.3 List Menu Items for Branch
GET http://localhost:8080/api/branches/1/menu-items?page=0&size=50
Authorization: Bearer YOUR_OWNER_TOKEN

### Expected: 200 OK, returns Page<BranchMenuItemResponse> with menu items for branchId=1 only

### 4.4 Get Single Menu Item
GET http://localhost:8080/api/branches/1/menu-items/1
Authorization: Bearer YOUR_OWNER_TOKEN

### Expected: 200 OK or 404 Not Found

### 4.5 Update Menu Item (change price or availability)
PUT http://localhost:8080/api/branches/1/menu-items/1
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer YOUR_OWNER_TOKEN

{
  "price": 16.50,
  "available": false
}

### Expected: 200 OK, returns updated BranchMenuItemResponse

### 4.6 Remove Product from Branch Menu
DELETE http://localhost:8080/api/branches/1/menu-items/1
Authorization: Bearer YOUR_OWNER_TOKEN

### Expected: 204 No Content

### 4.7 Tenant Isolation Test (should fail for other business)
### After creating a second business with different branchId, accessing branchId=1 should fail
GET http://localhost:8080/api/branches/1/menu-items
Authorization: Bearer OTHER_BUSINESS_TOKEN

### Expected: 403 Forbidden (you don't have access to this branch)

---

### ============================================================================
### ENDPOINT GROUP 5: BRANCH INVENTORY STOCK
### ============================================================================
### API Route: /api/branches/{branchId}/inventory/stocks
### Entity: BranchIngredientStock (branch_id + ingredient_id, branch-scoped, uses optimistic locking)
### This is where per-branch ingredient quantities are managed

### Prerequisites:
### - Ingredient must exist in catalog (from endpoint group 2)
### - Branch must exist in system
### - Current user's branchId must match or user is OWNER

### 5.1 Add Ingredient Stock to Branch
POST http://localhost:8080/api/branches/1/inventory/stocks
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer YOUR_OWNER_TOKEN

{
  "ingredientId": 1,
  "stockQuantity": 1000.000
}

### Expected: 201 Created, returns BranchStockResponse with branchId, ingredientId, stockQuantity, version=1

### 5.2 Add more ingredients to stock
POST http://localhost:8080/api/branches/1/inventory/stocks
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer YOUR_OWNER_TOKEN

{
  "ingredientId": 2,
  "stockQuantity": 500.000
}

---

POST http://localhost:8080/api/branches/1/inventory/stocks
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer YOUR_OWNER_TOKEN

{
  "ingredientId": 3,
  "stockQuantity": 200.000
}

### 5.3 List Stock for Branch
GET http://localhost:8080/api/branches/1/inventory/stocks?page=0&size=50
Authorization: Bearer YOUR_OWNER_TOKEN

### Expected: 200 OK, returns Page<BranchStockResponse> with stocks for branchId=1 only

### 5.4 Get Single Stock Record
GET http://localhost:8080/api/branches/1/inventory/stocks/1
Authorization: Bearer YOUR_OWNER_TOKEN

### Expected: 200 OK or 404 Not Found

### 5.5 Update Stock Quantity (with optimistic locking)
PUT http://localhost:8080/api/branches/1/inventory/stocks/1
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer YOUR_OWNER_TOKEN

{
  "stockQuantity": 950.000,
  "version": 1
}

### Expected: 200 OK, returns updated BranchStockResponse with version=2
### Note: If version is incorrect (concurrent update), returns 409 Conflict (OptimisticLockException)

### 5.6 Delete Stock Record
DELETE http://localhost:8080/api/branches/1/inventory/stocks/1
Authorization: Bearer YOUR_OWNER_TOKEN

### Expected: 204 No Content
### Note: Will fail (409 Conflict) if stockQuantity > 0

### 5.7 Tenant Isolation Test (should fail for other business)
GET http://localhost:8080/api/branches/1/inventory/stocks
Authorization: Bearer OTHER_BUSINESS_TOKEN

### Expected: 403 Forbidden (you don't have access to this branch)

---

### ============================================================================
### ERROR SCENARIOS (for comprehensive testing)
### ============================================================================

### E1: Invalid Authorization
GET http://localhost:8080/api/products
Authorization: Bearer INVALID_TOKEN

### Expected: 401 Unauthorized

### E2: Tenant Isolation Violation (view other business's product)
GET http://localhost:8080/api/products/999
Authorization: Bearer OTHER_BUSINESS_TOKEN

### Expected: 404 Not Found (returns as if product doesn't exist for security)

### E3: Branch Access Violation (non-owner accessing other branch)
GET http://localhost:8080/api/branches/2/menu-items
Authorization: Bearer BRANCH_1_STAFF_TOKEN

### Expected: 403 Forbidden (staff can only access their own branch)

### E4: Duplicate Menu Item
POST http://localhost:8080/api/branches/1/menu-items
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer YOUR_OWNER_TOKEN

{
  "productId": 1,
  "price": 20.00,
  "available": true
}

### Expected: 409 Conflict (product already in menu for this branch)

### E5: Invalid Ingredient Unit Change (ingredient has recipes)
PUT http://localhost:8080/api/ingredients/1
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer YOUR_OWNER_TOKEN

{
  "name": "Vodka",
  "unit": "PIECE"
}

### Expected: 409 Conflict (cannot change unit - has active recipes/stock)

### E6: Delete Ingredient with Active Stock
DELETE http://localhost:8080/api/ingredients/1
Authorization: Bearer YOUR_OWNER_TOKEN

### Expected: 409 Conflict (ingredient has active stock in branches)

### E7: Delete Stock with Non-zero Quantity
DELETE http://localhost:8080/api/branches/1/inventory/stocks/1
Authorization: Bearer YOUR_OWNER_TOKEN

### Expected: 409 Conflict (stock quantity must be 0 before deletion)

---

