### ============================================================================
### NOTES FOR INTEGRATION TESTING
### ============================================================================

### Database Setup:
### - DDL-auto is set to 'update', so tables are auto-created on startup
### - No seed data is included; all data is created via API calls
### - Each test should be independent (can run in any order)

### Concurrency Testing (for Sprint 2):
### - Use version numbers in BranchStockResponse to simulate concurrent updates
### - First client updates with version=1, gets back version=2
### - Second client tries to update with version=1, gets 409 Conflict
### - This tests optimistic locking (prepared for stock deduction in Sprint 2)

### Tenant/Branch Isolation Testing:
### - Create two businesses with separate owner accounts
### - Create branches under each business
### - Verify that staff from Business A cannot access Business B's products/branches
### - Verify that Owner can access all branches (branchId = null in JWT)

### Schema Notes:
### - Old columns: Product.price, Ingredient.stock_quantity still exist in DB (not dropped by Hibernate)
### - These columns are ignored by application (not mapped to entity fields)
### - In production, use explicit migration script to drop unused columns

### Known Limitations (Sprint 1):
### - No bulk recipe/stock operations (single-item API only)
### - No soft delete for Ingredient (hard delete only, blocked by references)
### - StockTransfer entity exists but logic is deferred to Sprint 2
### - No OptimisticLockException handler (will return 500 instead of 409 in concurrent scenarios)
